			<div class="content" id="post-content-4161201">
									

<p>This is a brutally long piece, but its Kafkaesque depiction of Dennis Huang's deterioration genuinely made me believe that he could snap the way he did. Two major notes of criticism: Dennis's use of 'Doc' in the second tab made me roll my eyes &#8212; when was the last time you ever called someone Doc &#8212; and in-universe, blackboxing the name of the medications that are used to treat SCP-4504 in the containment procedures is bafflingly idiotic. How is the Foundation supposed to treat Dennis if nobody knows what he's supposed to be treated with?</p>

							</div>

								
