															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="4504036"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1550817999 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Feb 2019 06:46</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4161228">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Dr Weber: Now really, Dennis. You cannot keep things like this to yourself. You must talk to me about them, it’s what I’m here for.</p>
<p>SCP-4504: No, Doc, please- huhh, don’t interrupt me. I’m- It’s hard to concentrate.</p>
<p>Dr Weber: What the devil is the matter with you?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Pushed me out of the immersion given Weber changes from 0 to 1 when the plot wants him to.</p>
<p>Reread it two times so I could be sure it wasn't my eyes or something but I don't really get why Weber states &quot;what the devil is the matter with you.&quot; If its to convey impatience or lording over the patient, I don't really get that from the overall character of Weber as he's somewhat of a blank slate filled with the goals of the Foundation itself. To protect coldly.</p>
<p>Maybe if I believed Weber wasn't just a foil for Dennis and had his own ambitions leading up to the tone shift, I would upvote it. As it stands, it's a solid piece but doesn't sit well with me in terms of narrative inconsistency.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">The&nbsp;Pros&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;piece.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">&gt;&gt;&gt;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>EDIT: I think its something very small that only bugs me, and I do hope this does well with others. It has a solid progression, the confessions of Dennis only make his situation worse, its very clear that the Foundation's protocols are noncompatible with the humanoid's condition and have only exaggerated his mental illness rather than calm him down to a restful or amicable state.</p>
<p>EDIT-EDIT:</p>
<p>Minor SpaGR issues I detected</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Haven’t had a suicidal though all week</p>
</blockquote>
<p>thought*</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After being returning to its containment cell prematurely</p>
</blockquote>
<p>returned*</p>
<p>And another huge logic issue I picked up on the third reading. Why is the Foundation putting this anomaly near other humanoids?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>freeing two dozen other humanoid SCP objects. Among those that breached containment were SCP-4504 and SCP-082.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems like it happens far too often then it should. Like, the way it escapes and the way it attempts suicide are fine and fun because you can see the cogworks in Dennis' head as he responds to every situation. But the fact he's constantly near other humanoids? It makes the Foundation seem extremely inept and piles onto the weird inconsistencies from beforehand with Weber's impatience.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>TL;DR: I want to reiterate, I reread this four times because I loved the direction and premise. Truly, I really do want to upvote this on wikidot after a few changes.</p>

							</div>

								
