			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4161247">
									

<p>It's one thing for the tests and oversecurity to be done, but man, that Site must be pretty terrible if there are other people like Dr. Weber working there. His dialog seems cold in a flatly-written way, rather than in a realistic way. Normally I wouldn't examine that aspect too much, but he's a central character here, and although there's clearly an angle being built there with him, I also can't help but wonder if the article's also painting him as just a regular dude that happened to totally break a man due to how he comes off from the dialog.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I like it, on the assumption that you were writing to tell us a story about particularly cruel and uncaring Foundation researchers breaking an anomaly because they see him as one (which is how I read it and like to believe you wrote it).</span> EDIT: A thing I noticed as it went on was that 4504 shifted in personality to cracking jokes and sarcasm, and I don't mind this inherently, but I dunno. It felt off here, almost like a completely different character from another article.</p>
<p>I still like the core concept and where you take this at a number of points, but I think the flat characterization/dialog for me on the whole overshadows what I like about it, enough to downvote. But good job going for this all the same! Longform pieces with a sense of clarity and direction are always cool as heck and you went for a concept I haven't seen explored much on the site.</p>

							</div>

								
