														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4166273">
									

<p>The reason I mentioned Pelican Bay is to establish that the way they treated him, which you rightly call torture, is considered best practice in one of the largest facilities of its kind in the world. The Foundation psychiatric staff were being trained professionals in treating incarcerated humans, not incompetents.</p>
<p>The idea that sort of treatment is a monstrous abrogation of the responsibilities of mental health care and custodial detention both is only very slowly and very recently starting to circulate in anything approaching the mainstream (in the anglosphere, at least) which is part of why the progression of time in the piece is so important.</p>
<p>The piece is doing what a lot of good scifi tends to do and place a real issue at a slight distance to better illuminate the problems with an aspect of the world we currently live in.</p>

